The Difference CFG algorithm implemented here is a port of the
DifferenceCFG_PreCFG node from that project. The following files contain
code derived from the upstream work:

  sd_webui_difference_cfg/core.py

Specifically, interpolated_scales() and the body of the pre-CFG patch are
ported without algorithmic change. The absolute_sum L1-norm ratio, both
division-by-zero guards, the fallback_weight computation, the min-max
normalisation of the absolute difference and the squared / root exponent
branches all follow the upstream implementation.


MODIFICATIONS
=============

The following changes were made to the upstream work in the course of
porting it to Forge-derived Stable Diffusion WebUIs. None of them alter the
algorithm itself.

  * Ported from a ComfyUI node class to a WebUI Script extension. The
    ComfyUI node schema is replaced by a Gradio UI, and model patching goes
    through forge_objects.unet rather than a cloned ComfyUI model object.

  * Added a Forge Neo code path. Forge Neo's pre-CFG hook fires before model
    evaluation with a positional argument tuple, which is incompatible with
    the dict / conds_out signature the upstream node expects, so on that
    backend the extension registers a post-CFG hook instead and reconstructs
    the equivalent result. Where sd-webui-TCFG is active and ordered ahead of
    this extension, the post-CFG path reads the damped unconditional
    prediction TCFG stashes in model_options; otherwise it falls back to the
    raw unconditional prediction.

  * Added priority-based hook insertion. Forge-derived backends append
    pre-CFG hooks in registration order, which is effectively alphabetical
    and varies with the set of installed extensions. This extension inserts
    itself at priority 14.2 so that the assembled chain does not depend on
    what else happens to be present.

  * Added a chain dump, emitted at sampling time when the environment
    variable SD_WEBUI_SETI_DEBUG is set to 1, replacing the upstream node's
    ANSI-coloured startup print.

  * Extended the Reference CFG range from the upstream maximum of 10 to 20,
    to cover high-CFG workflows where the reference target itself needs to
    sit above the usual 5 to 10 range.

  * Replaced the direct model_sampling.percent_to_sigma() call with a helper
    that resolves the sigma schedule across the supported backends.

  * Converted the sigma argument to a Python float through a helper rather
    than indexing the tensor directly.

  * Added PNG infotext round-trip support using the DiffCFG key prefix, and
    XYZ Grid axes for the enabled flag and the method dropdown.

  * Added exception handling around the hook so that an internal failure
    returns the unmodified standard CFG output rather than aborting
    generation.

  * Split the algorithm out of sd-webui-SkimmedCFG into this repository. The
    upstream project ships DifferenceCFG_PreCFG alongside the skimming nodes
    in a single file; this extension carries only the Difference CFG
    algorithm and none of the shared masking helpers.
